{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnConstruction","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.MarkovTrace"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.exists_indistinguishable_by_every_traceFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.exists_indistinguishable_by_every_traceFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L302-L319","doc":"**Every trace-factoring functional is blind to it.** The Markov trace\nincluded — which is the point, since that is the functional the `(2,1)` clause\nroutes through. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.trace_does_not_separate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.trace_does_not_separate","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L270-L300","doc":"**The block traces do not separate decompositions.** Whenever a block has\ndimension at least 2 there are distinct decompositions with *every* block trace\nequal — so every trace-factoring functional, the Markov trace included, takes the\nsame value on both. The witness is an off-diagonal matrix unit, which is\ntraceless. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockAt_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockAt_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L267-L268","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockAt_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockAt_self","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L264-L265","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockAt","kind":"def","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L257-L262","doc":"The decomposition carrying a single matrix on block `lam`, zero elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.markovTraceOnWedderburn_eq_traceFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.markovTraceOnWedderburn_eq_traceFunctional","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L222-L227","doc":"The Markov trace is itself such a functional, with `c = y_·(q_0)`. So the\nno-go applies to it, not merely to an abstract family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.three_supported_traceFunctionals_dependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.three_supported_traceFunctionals_dependent","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L201-L220","doc":"**Any three are linearly dependent.** So volume, surface and Coulomb cannot\nbe three independent trace-factoring functionals localised at a single\npartition: the span is one-dimensional, and three vectors in a line are\ndependent. The witness is explicit, not an existence argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.traceFunctional_supported_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.traceFunctional_supported_apply","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L189-L199","doc":"**A functional supported at one partition is one real times one real.** All\nthe freedom it has is the single coefficient `c lam`; the decomposition enters\nonly through the single number `(x lam).trace`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.traceFunctional_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.traceFunctional_injective","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L169-L187","doc":"Distinct coefficient families give distinct functionals. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.traceFunctional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.traceFunctional","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L164-L167","doc":"A functional that factors through the block traces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.coeff_eq_of_markovTrace_eq_regular_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.coeff_eq_of_markovTrace_eq_regular_trace","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L104-L126","doc":"**Sharpness.** If the Markov trace agrees with the regular trace on *every*\ndecomposition, the coefficients were the dimensions all along. So any genuine\n`q`-deformation of `y_λ` is visible on some element — the bridge is not a\nrestatement of the regular trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockOne_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockOne_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L99-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockOne_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockOne_self","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L93-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.blockOne","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L84-L91","doc":"**The single-block indicator.** `blockOne lam` is the decomposition carrying\nthe identity matrix on block `lam` and zero elsewhere; its block trace is `f^λ`\nat `lam` and `0` away from it. This is what turns \"the two traces agree on every\n`x`\" into a statement about the coefficients themselves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.markovTrace_eq_regular_trace_of_coeff_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.markovTrace_eq_regular_trace_of_coeff_eq","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L69-L82","doc":"If the Jones–Markov coefficients are the seminormal dimensions, the Markov\ntrace *is* the regular trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.markovTrace_sub_regular_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeAlgebra.WedderburnTrace.markovTrace_sub_regular_trace","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HeckeAlgebra/WedderburnTrace.lean#L53-L67","doc":"**The Markov trace is the regular trace with deformed coefficients.** The\ndifference collapses to a single sum over partitions in which the algebra plays\nno part — only `y_λ(q_0) − f^λ` does. ","signatureChunk":0}]}